      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>PR for the webac ontology changes:<br/>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo-webac-ontology/pull/1\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo-webac-ontology/pull/1</a></p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=6089a48d248ef60073948d92\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"6089a48d248ef60073948d92\" data-account-id=\"6089a48d248ef60073948d92\" accountid=\"6089a48d248ef60073948d92\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Unknown</a>, looking at your implementation of rolesHavePermissions in WebACAuthorizationDelegate.</p>\n\n<p>It seems to rely on only one action for each permission, but with Update, Delete and Append these will overlap Write. Or at least they would in my mind. So I am looking at your logic <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo-module-auth-webac/blob/master/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/auth/webac/WebACAuthorizationDelegate.java#L113-L117\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">here</a>.</p>\n\n<p>Would it be adequate to reverse the flow and compare the roles provided to see if they give the actions requested (instead of the current opposite)?</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo-module-auth-webac/compare/master...whikloj:fcrepo-1794?expand=1\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">Here is a link</a> to the comparison of my changes so far. The important one is how we manage the actionMap?</p>",
     "created": "28/Oct/15 12:52 AM",
     "id": "15586",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11704/comment/15586",
